{"raw": {"https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5518282/assistant-professor-environmental-geologist": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Environmental Geologist", "description": "Assistant Professor, Environmental Geologist Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00525 Division Academic Affairs Department Biology & Earth Science Opening Date 10/15/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University invites applications for the position of a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor of Earth Science with a primary specialization in Environmental Geology. We seek candidates who will contribute to the department\u2019s efforts to enhance diversity and provide an inclusive learning environment for all. RESPONSIBILITIES RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach 21 workload hours in the academic year including: Introduction to Environmental Science lecture & lab, Physical Geology lecture & lab, Environmental Geology lecture & lab, and Hydrology lecture & lab. Contribute to university life through student advising, service on university and departmental committees, and developing an active research program that incorporates undergraduate research students. Direct the Environmental Science program. QUALIFICATIONS QUALIFICATIONS: PhD is required for this full-time, tenure track position. Strong candidates will be broadly trained in environmental geology and environmental science. Evidence of effective teaching in environmental science lecture and lab courses is required. Strong publication record is required. The candidate must demonstrate an active research agenda that can include undergraduate students, excellence in undergraduate teaching, and experience in mentoring students. Preference will be given to individuals with prior experience in developing and teaching environmental science courses at the introductory and upper levels. COMPENSATION : For the rank of Assistant Professor - $62,226 (plus full University benefits). START DATE: This appointment begins in August 2027. APPLICATION: To apply: submit a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, a teaching philosophy statement, contact information for three (3) references, research plan statement and how your plan can incorporate undergraduate students, and a statement consisting of no more than one single-spaced page, addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein\u2019s belonging plan? Preference given to applicants who submit materials by November 30, 2026. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION DEPARTMENT: The Department consists of approximately 300 students, 9 full-time and 9 part-time faculty, a laboratory coordinator and an administrative assistant. It offers majors in: Environmental Science, Biology, and Zoo & Conservation Science, including an Aquarium Track. Many of our faculty and students are also involved with interdisciplinary programs in Biochemistry & Molecular Biology and Sustainability. The Department is an active participant in the Integrative Studies Program and offers global education travel courses. Visit us at https://www.otterbein.edu/biology-earth-science/ to learn more about the Department of Biology & Earth Science and the Biology, Environmental Science, and Zoo & Conservation Science majors. OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio\u2019s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein is the first university in Ohio to be selected by the American Association of Colleges and Universities to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE : Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine\u2019s Top 100 list of America\u2019s \u201cBest Places to Live\u201d and recognized as one of Forbes\u2019 \u201cAmerica\u2019s Friendliest Towns.\u201d Westerville has a population of approximately 37,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital, a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 1.4 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein University\u2019s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5518306/assistant-professor-anatomist-or-physiologist": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Anatomist or Physiologist", "description": "Assistant Professor, Anatomist or Physiologist Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00526 Division Academic Affairs Department Biology & Earth Science Opening Date 10/15/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University invites applications for the position of a full-time, tenure track or non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Biology with a primary specialization in Human Anatomy & Physiology. We seek candidates with a who will contribute to the department\u2019s efforts to enhance diversity and provide an inclusive learning environment for all. RESPONSIBILITIES RESPONSIBILITIES: If non-tenure track: teach 24 workload hours in the academic year including: Anatomy & Physiology I labs, Anatomy & Physiology II lectures, Anatomy & Physiology II labs, and an Integrative Studies course in their field of expertise. Serve as Lab Director, responsible for organizing the lab, preparing student learning materials and assessments, and directing all A&P instructors, for all Anatomy & Physiology I labs. Contribute to university life through advising pre-professional health students and service on university and departmental committees. If tenure track: teach 21 workload hours in the academic year and engage in an active research program along with the other listed responsibilities. An individual on the tenure track would teach 1 less A&P lab than in the non-tenure track route. COMPENSATION : For the rank of Assistant Professor - $62,226 (plus full University benefits). START DATE: This appointment begins in August 2027. QUALIFICATIONS QUALIFICATIONS: PhD, MD, or DO is required for this full-time, tenure track or non-tenure track position. A strong candidate will be a broadly trained anatomist, physiologist, or in a closely related field, with expertise in human anatomy and physiology and health. All candidates need to provide evidence of teaching effectiveness in anatomy and physiology lectures and labs and display a commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Preference will be given to candidates with more than 3 years\u2019 experience teaching human anatomy and physiology labs and lectures. Candidates for the tenure track option should have a strong publication record and an active research plan that can include undergraduate students. Please clearly indicate if you are applying for a tenure track or non-tenure track position. APPLICATION: To apply: submit a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, a teaching philosophy statement, contact information for three (3) references, and a statement consisting of no more than one single-spaced page, addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein\u2019s belonging plan? If you are applying for a tenure track position, please submit a research plan statement and how your plan can incorporate undergraduate students. Preference given to applicants who submit materials by November 30, 2026. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION DEPARTMENT: The Department consists of approximately 300 students, 9 full-time and 9 part-time faculty, a laboratory coordinator, and an administrative assistant. It offers majors in: Biology, Zoo & Conservation Science, and Environmental Science. Many of our faculty and students are also involved with interdisciplinary programs in Biochemistry & Molecular Biology and Sustainability. The Department is an active participant in the Integrative Studies Program and offers global education travel courses. Visit us at https://www.otterbein.edu/biology-earth-science/ to learn more about the Department of Biology & Earth Science and our majors. OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio\u2019s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein is the first university in Ohio to be selected by the American Association of Colleges and Universities to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE : Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine\u2019s Top 100 list of America\u2019s \u201cBest Places to Live\u201d and recognized as one of Forbes\u2019 \u201cAmerica\u2019s Friendliest Towns.\u201d Westerville has a population of approximately 37,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital, a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 1.4 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein University\u2019s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5519168/assistant-professor-business-administration-management": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Business Administration/Management", "description": "Assistant Professor, Business Administration/Management Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty Job Number 00527 Division Academic Affairs Department Business/Accounting/Economics Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University invites applications for the position of a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor of Management. We seek candidates who will contribute to the department\u2019s efforts to enhance diversity and provide an inclusive learning environment for all. RESPONSIBILITIES RESPONSIBILITIES: The candidate is expected to excel in the areas of teaching, scholarship, research and service related to Otterbein\u2019s bachelor\u2019s degree in Business Administration and Management. Teaching responsibilities will be primarily in Principles of Management (Writing Intensive), Personnel/Human Resource Management, Leadership and Culture, Training and Development, and Business and Society. Research responsibilities include publishing in peer-reviewed journals and presenting research at peer-reviewed conferences in business administration, management, or related fields. Faculty members are also expected to be involved in professional and community activities for the purposes of scholarship, professional development, student advising and mentorship, and service. COMPENSATION : For the rank of Assistant Professor (terminal degree) - $71,500 (plus full University benefits). If initial appointment is at the rank of Instructor - $62,000 (plus full University benefits). WHEN: This appointment will begin August 2027. QUALIFICATIONS QUALIFICATIONS: A PhD or DBA in a business discipline from an Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB) accredited university with a specialization in Management is required. Candidates who are ABD will be considered if they are within one year of completing their doctoral degree. Effective teaching experience at the baccalaureate level and demonstrated record of scholarship is also required. The ideal candidate must possess superior communication, leadership and organization skills, and an ability to work effectively with students, faculty and staff from diverse communities and cultures. This is a tenure-track position with commensurate expectations for teaching, scholarship, and service. Candidates who have not completed their terminal degree at the time of appointment will be appointed at the rank of instructor on a non-tenure track basis. APPLICATION: To apply: submit a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, a teaching philosophy statement, contact information for three references, research statement, and a statement consisting of no more than one single-spaced page addressing the following two questions: How has a focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion informed your teaching, scholarship, and/or professional experience to date? How do you see yourself contributing to Otterbein\u2019s belonging plan? Preference given to applicants who submit materials by November 19, 2026. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION DEPARTMENT: The Department of Business, Accounting & Economics is composed of 9 full-time faculty and 7 part-time faculty. Majors offered: a B.S. in Accounting, Business Administration & Management, Business Analytics, Finance and Marketing as well as a B.A. in Economics (Changing to Environmental Economics and Sustainability in July 2027). Minors offered: Accounting, Business Administration, Economics, International Business & Management, Finance, Marketing, Marketing Analytics. The department is dedicated to providing a personalized education of distinction that leads our graduates to inquiring, ethical, humane, and productive lives as global citizens. The faculty is focused on action-oriented learning by integrating classroom knowledge with practice through internships, research, service projects, study abroad, participation in professional associations, and networking with employers, faculty, alumni, community leaders, and recruiters. To learn about all the programs offered in the Department of Business, Accounting & Economics, please visit https://www.otterbein.edu/business-accounting-economics/. OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY : Historically progressive. That is the hallmark of Otterbein University and those connected to this private university nestled in the picturesque, historic Uptown Westerville district in central Ohio and minutes away from Columbus, Ohio\u2019s largest city. Otterbein has set the pace by providing an educational experience that is progressive, innovative, and inclusive. Students come from towns throughout Ohio, as well as many states and multiple countries, enriching the campus through their individual and collective diversity. As a university that educates students of various racial, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds, we strive for and value a diverse faculty and staff that reflects our student population and Franklin County. Otterbein has been selected as one of 23 universities across the US and the first in Ohio to host a Truth, Racial Healing and Transformation Campus Center. Otterbein will work with its own campus community as well as the Columbus City and Westerville City school districts to create positive narrative change about race; promote racial healing activities; and erase structural barriers to equity and opportunity. Otterbein University is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission (HLC) and is a member of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. For more than a decade, Otterbein has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report for its academic quality. In the 2025\u20132026 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Otterbein ranked #12 among 160 Regional Universities in the Midwest. To learn more about Otterbein, visit www.otterbein.edu . WHERE : Otterbein University is located in Westerville, Ohio, a suburb of Columbus, and has received notable national designations, including two appearances on Money Magazine\u2019s Top 100 list of Americas\u2019 \u201cBest Places to Live\u201d and recognized as one of Forbes \u201cAmerica\u2019s Friendliest Towns.\u201d Westerville has a population of approximately 38,000 people and combines the beauty and convenience of a medium-sized community with the cultural, educational, and economic benefits of Columbus, the state capital; a thriving and diverse metropolitan area of 2.2 million people. Central Ohio is the fastest growing area in the state with stability provided by a diversified economy. Otterbein University\u2019s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ? ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: ? https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ ? Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply"}}, "rows": {"https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5518282/assistant-professor-environmental-geologist": {"school_id": 1074, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5518282/assistant-professor-environmental-geologist", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor, Environmental Geologist", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Environmental Geologist; environmental science lecture", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5518306/assistant-professor-anatomist-or-physiologist": {"school_id": 1074, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5518306/assistant-professor-anatomist-or-physiologist", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor, Anatomist or Physiologist", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Biology & Earth Science and our majors", "area_key_words": "Anatomist or Physiologist", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5519168/assistant-professor-business-administration-management": {"school_id": 1074, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein/jobs/5519168/assistant-professor-business-administration-management", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor, Business Administration/Management", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Business Administration/Management", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}}, "school_id": 1074, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-19T20:19:54+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-19T20:19:54+00:00", "last_error": ""}